Key lessons
- Dominant "unknown" compiled allocator traffic was mostly `wnf_dup_nod` clones.
- Attribution coverage is now strong enough to prioritize optimization work with confidence.
- Remaining major heap pressures are still `TERM_OP2` and `AOT_DUP_CELL` on arithmetic-heavy workloads.

Likely next steps
1) Reduce `TERM_OP2` materialization in strict compiled contexts by unboxing strict numeric OP2 paths to direct NUM results.
2) Attack `WNF_DUP_NOD` pressure by reducing non-copy-free DUP forcing/materialization frequency (while preserving DUP/SUP semantics).
3) Consider adding a shared header/inc for heap-kind ids to avoid include-order coupling between `heap/alloc.c` and `aot/_.c`.
